WEBVTT

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.206
They loaded four months
of food in Sydney.

00:00:20.206 --> 00:00:22.181
If the Grafton was still missing then,

00:00:22.181 --> 00:00:24.006
friends would send help.

00:00:24.006 --> 00:00:27.595
Five men sailed south
for Campbell Island in search of tin.

00:00:31.154 --> 00:00:32.759
They found no tin.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.884
On New Year’s Day the Grafton
entered Carnley Harbour.

00:00:35.884 --> 00:00:39.499
Twenty fathoms of line hung beside
the cliffs without touching bottom.

00:00:42.252 --> 00:00:45.337
An anchor chain snapped
at seven the next evening.

00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:47.912
Each swell brought
the schooner nearer the rocks.

00:00:47.912 --> 00:00:49.352
At midnight she struck.

00:00:51.654 --> 00:00:54.037
Pieces of keel floated past.

00:00:54.037 --> 00:00:56.787
The men abandoned the pumps
to save their food.

00:00:56.787 --> 00:01:00.250
A quarter of an hour later the sea
had reached the cabin table.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.257
In daylight all five reached the beach.

00:01:04.257 --> 00:01:06.357
Thomas Musgrave, François Raynal,

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:09.632
Alick McLaren, Henry Forgés
and George Harris.

00:01:09.632 --> 00:01:11.693
Their boat survived the landing too.

00:01:13.314 --> 00:01:15.036
Raynal was ill.

00:01:15.036 --> 00:01:17.011
He walked a hundred yards that day,

00:01:17.011 --> 00:01:20.259
from the beach to their shelter
under the Grafton’s own mainsail.

